  "claim_short": "Full counterexample to the equality characterization in Conjecture 4.1 of arXiv:1612.01128. Take K=[-1/2,1/2]x[-2,2]x[-3,3] and Lambda=diag(0,1,-1). For every s in [0,1], e^{s Lambda}K intersect B_2^3 is exactly the fixed spherical slab where |x_1| is at most 1/2, because the other half-widths are at least 2 and 3/e. Hence phi(s)=11pi/12 throughout the interval and midpoint equality holds at t=1, although neither K...",
